order to avoid having a huge insurance burden to lay off? Firm 1 sells you
$X of insurance on the terms you suggest. Firm 2 agrees to pay firm 1 50%
of your medical bills, in exchange for a premium from you. As long as the
two firms cannot conspire and firm 1 cannot conspire with the health
providers (a little harder to guarantee), the effect is almost exactly as
if you bought $2x of insurance. The one difference is that the insurance
firm will skimp on expenses that are not reimbursable by firm 2, such as
research on which doctor to assign you to.

